.TH ciaaw_s2z 3 "30 August 2026" "1.3.2" "Library calls"

.SH NAME
\"{{{
s2z \- get the atomic number
\"}}}

.SH LIBRARY
\"{{{
ciaaw library 
.RI ( libciaaw ", " \-lciaaw )
\"}}}

.SH SYNOPSIS
\"{{{
.IP Fortran 10
.BI "function s2z(" s ")result(res)"
.RS
.IP "" 3
.BI "character(len=*), intent(in)  :: " s    
.IP "" 3
.BI "integer(int32)  :: " res                
.RE

.IP C 10
.BI "int ciaaw_s2z(char *" s, "int " n,  ");"

\"}}}

.SH DESCRIPTION
Get the atomic number \fBZ\fP of the element \fIs\fP.

Arguments:
.IP \fIs\fP 10
Element symbol.

.SH RETURN VALUE
.IP -1 10  
If the element does not have an ICE.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ciaaw (3),
.BR ciaaw_cli (1),
.BR ciaaw_version (3),
.BR ciaaw_saw (3),
.BR ciaaw_ice (3),
.BR ciaaw_nice (3),
.BR ciaaw_naw (3), 
.BR ciaaw_nnaw (3),
.BR ciaaw_ices (3),
.BR ciaaw_naws (3),
.BR ciaaw_s2z (3)
